kvarn-varlen: fingerprint the KVarN KV and GDN state each step reads; flag the invariants.

Research experiment for the kvarn-varlen item (docs/research/deepinfer/README.md, "Blocker
for E"). NOT in patches/series. Written against the image's installed (already patched)
vLLM 0.31.0, whose v1/attention/backends/kvarn_attn.py is kvarn/files' copy.

Adds v1/kvv_fp.py and four hook sites, all behind VLLM_KVV_FP=<file> (unset = inert):
  - kvarn_attn.note_scheduled_blocks: a t=sched record per real step (scheduler view).
  - KVarNMetadataBuilder.build (target model's builder only, real steps only, never
    during capture): after each flush, layer 0's tile bit-sums are recorded; after the
    allocate pass, a t=kv record per request with the committed length, per-layer exact
    bit-sums of everything attention reads below it, and the flags
      H3  committed (seq_len - query_len) != scheduler num_computed_tokens
      H4  a pool tile is read over rows its current slot lifetime never wrote
      H5  an int4 tile below committed changed since KVarN flushed it
  - MambaHybridModelState.preprocess_state (align mode, after the pre-copy): a t=gdn
    record per request with the window base, num_accepted, pre-copy source, per GDN layer
    bit-sums of the SSM / conv state the step starts from, and the flags
      H2_back   window base column moved down (seq_len = committed + q_len fell)
      H2_reloc  pre-copy source column now names a different physical block than the
                previous step's table did (scheduler relocated it in between)
      H2_null   the step starts from the null block
Syncs every step: debugging arm only. VLLM_KVV_FP_TILES=0 drops the per-tile list.

